RODE optional Codex runtime
==========================

This package supplies a pinned upstream native Codex executable and its license
notices. Install it alongside rode to enable automatic runtime discovery, or
configure your own executable in RODE's agent settings. No Node.js/npm is needed.

Use `rode --codex login` to authenticate and `rode --codex --version` to inspect
the runtime. For SSH projects, RODE copies a matching runtime to a private cache
on the project host on first use. Credentials remain on that host; tools obey
the active project sandbox.

The runtime is versioned separately from the editor. Updates must pass RODE's
protocol compatibility checks. Package installation does not sign in, download
models, start a service or change user preferences. An installed compatible
Codex can also be used without this optional package.
